      "claim": "The spec's `touches` names `saffron/cell/session.py` and `saffron/ledger.py`, both listed under `.saffron/policy.yaml`'s `elevate_on`, so this task auto-elevates to `risk: elevated`, where the `size` gate is blocking at the `feature` ceiling of 3000 changed tokens. `estimated_lines: 249` with `estimate_measured: true` causes the host-side pre-check to trust the figure directly (996 tokens at the 4-tokens/line heuristic), comfortably under the ceiling and even under the 80% warning line, so the pre-check would raise no concern. But the immediately preceding, similarly-shaped spec in this stack, SA-0205 (also `estimate_measured: true`, estimated at 297 lines), landed roughly 2-3x that figure in its merged diff even restricted to its own `touches` files, and criterion 2 here demands a single witness driving four distinct turn-endings across five event kinds, null/absent counts, and three unpriced-model cases in one test - a noticeably larger surface than anything SA-0205's criteria asked for - plus five other new witnesses and one pre-existing test to repair. If the real build lands anywhere near SA-0205's actual overrun ratio, real changed tokens (computed by genuine tokenization, plausibly higher per line than the heuristic for dense Python) could approach or clear 3000, at which point `size` blocks a cell that otherwise built every criterion correctly, after money was already spent. This names no single acceptance criterion.",
